ing a SCADA system must have a written\n354:operator’s plan must include provisions to:\n378:(a) General. This section applies to each operator of a pipeline facility with a\n380:pipeline facility through a SCADA system. Each operator must have and follow\n386:\f(h) Training. Each operator must establish a controller training program and\n389:operator’s program must provide for training each controller to carry out the\n390:roles and responsibilities defined by the operator. In addition, the training\n394:other individuals, defined by the operator, who would reasonably be expected\n396:normal, abnormal or emergency situations. Operators must comply with the\n406:§ 195.505 Qualification program. Each operator shall have and follow a written qualification program. The program\n407:shall include provisions to:\n411:Vantage failed to qualify one controller under the US Operator Qualification (OQ)\n419:Onboarding, training and mentoring operators. US Operators are qualified in accordance\n426:Post inspection, the operator provided qualification records that met the requirements of\n427:the operators US Operator Qualification Plan. No further action required.\n469:Notice.\n477:\fResponse to this Notice\n478:Enclosed as part of this Notice is a document entitled Response Options for Pipeline Operators\n486:Following your receipt of this Notice, you have 30 days to respond as described in the enclosed\n487:Response Options. If you do not respond within 30 days of receipt of this Notice, this constitutes\n488:a waiver of your right to contest the allegations in this Notice and authorizes the Associate\n489:Administrator for Pipeline Safety to find facts as alleged in this Notice without further notice to\n490:you and to issue a Final Order. If you are responding to this Notice, we propose that you submit\n491:your correspondence to my office within 30 days from receipt of this Notice. The Region\n510:Response Options for Pipeline Operators in Enforcement Proceedings\n523:In 